From 23439c9f85124d25a587443ab6aa5de5e51ffb7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: resolve FW_URI into a cached FW_FILE for regression
 runs (#980)

When FW_FILE is not set, the regression wrappers now fetch the image named
by FW_URI (http, https or file) and use the cached copy as FW_FILE. FW_FILE
keeps working unchanged for local images.

scripts/lib/fw_resolve.py keys the cache by the SHA-256 of the full URI, so
two URIs with the same file name never share an entry. The download goes to
a temporary file in the cache directory and is renamed into place only after
the optional FW_SHA256 check passes and the file is non-empty, so a failed
download is never served as a cache hit.

scripts/lib/test_fw_resolve.py covers reuse, URI collisions, failed and
empty downloads, SHA-256 mismatch and unsupported schemes.
